===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|fraghten}}, {{m|enm|fraughten}}, {{m|enm|freghten}}, from {{der|en|dum|vrachten}}, {{m|dum|vrechten}}, from the noun (see above).

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete|_|except in past participle}} To [[load]] (a ship, cargo etc.).
#* '''1899''' or '''1590''', {{w|Christopher Marlowe}}, ''The Jew of Malta'', Act I, line 60:
#*: The ships are safe thou say'st, and richly '''fraught'''?
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To form the cargo of a vessel.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Tempest|text=Had I been any god of power, I would / Have sunk the sea within the earth, or e'er / It should the good ship so have swallow'd and / The '''fraughting''' souls within her.}}

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|of a cargo-carrier}} [[laden|Laden]].
#*{{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|II|viii|passage=a vessel of our country richly '''fraught'''}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|with ''with''}} [[loaded|Loaded]] up or [[charged]] with; accompanied by; [[entailing]].
#* {{RQ:South Twelve Sermons|passage=a discourse '''fraught''' with all the commending excellences of speech}}
#* '''a. 1865''', {{w|Isaac Taylor}}, ''Epidemic Whims''
#*: enterprises '''fraught''' with world-wide benefits
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1936|author=Rollo Ahmed|title=The Black Art|publisher=Long|location=London|page=22|passage=The simplest action was '''fraught''' with danger, and could only be accomplished with the aid of talismans and counter-spells[.]}}
#* '''2005''', [[w:Plato|Plato]], ''Sophist''. Translation by Lesley Brown. [[w:Stephanus pagination|236d]].
#*: {{...}} all these matters are '''fraught''' with paradox, just as they always have been
# {{lb|en|with ''with''}} Furnished, [[equipped]].
# [[distressed|Distressed]] or causing distress, for example through [[complexity]].
#: ''a '''fraught''' relationship; a '''fraught''' process''
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Oliver Brown| title=Oscar Pistorius jailed for five years – sport afforded no protection against his tragic fallibilities: Bladerunner's punishment for killing Reeva Steenkamp is but a frippery when set against the burden that her bereft parents, June and Barry, must carry &#91;print version: No room for sentimentality in this tragedy, 13 September 2014, p.&nbsp;S22&#93;|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/worldnews/oscar-pistorius/11089621/Oscar-Pistorius-jailed-for-five-years-sport-afforded-no-protection-against-his-tragic-fallibilities.html| work={{w|The Daily Telegraph}} (Sport)| date=21 October 2014| passage=But ever since the concept of "hamartia" recurred through Aristotle's ''Poetics'', in an attempt to describe man's ingrained iniquity, our impulse has been to identify a telling defect in those brought suddenly and dramatically low. With [[w:Oscar Pistorius|[Oscar] Pistorius]], that task is '''fraught'''.}}

